From: macos15-guest-stack <kirin@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] exec: yield between draws of a sync exec packet

A sync exec packet runs every draw of one position back to back on the
fixed executor, and on a heavy packet (a full-frame 1920x1080 Store at
RGBA16Float is ~8 MiB of readback plus guest writeback) that is the whole
of sync_exec_lock_hold.  Nothing about ordering requires the executor to
monopolise the host CPU while it waits on the GPU or copies bytes, so it
yields every 8 ms and lets the OS schedule the other guest vCPUs, the
window thread and the log writer.

This does not shorten the packet's own latency - the draws still run
serially in order - so it is a convoy relief, not a fix for the
guest-visible stall; the count and reason stay on sync_exec_lock_hold.

Apply on top of 0004 in the reims-vgpu source root:  patch -p1 < this file

diff --git a/crates/reims-vgpu/src/runtime/exec/mod.rs b/crates/reims-vgpu/src/runtime/exec/mod.rs
index 7c78b462..dcd77288 100644
--- a/crates/reims-vgpu/src/runtime/exec/mod.rs
+++ b/crates/reims-vgpu/src/runtime/exec/mod.rs
@@ -5232,7 +5232,23 @@ fn finish_stream<M: HostMemory + HostOps>(
         }
         let input_scope = draw::BufferSnapshotScope::new();
         let mut render_pass = crate::backend::selected().begin_render_pass();
+        // A sync exec packet runs every draw of one position back to back on the
+        // fixed executor, and on a heavy packet (a full-frame 1920x1080 Store at
+        // RGBA16Float is ~8 MiB of readback plus guest writeback, and the guest's
+        // GPU-restart watchdog prices a sync at native-GPU latency) that is the
+        // whole of `sync_exec_lock_hold`. Nothing about ordering requires the
+        // executor to monopolise the host CPU while it waits on the GPU or copies
+        // bytes: yielding between draws lets the OS schedule the other guest
+        // vCPUs, the window thread and the log writer. It does not shorten the
+        // packet's own latency - the draws still run serially in order - so this
+        // is a convoy relief, not a fix for the guest-visible stall; the count
+        // and reason stay on `sync_exec_lock_hold`.
+        let mut last_yield = std::time::Instant::now();
         for (di, pd) in draw_list.iter().enumerate() {
+            if last_yield.elapsed().as_millis() >= 8 {
+                std::thread::yield_now();
+                last_yield = std::time::Instant::now();
+            }
             fin.enter(crate::runtime::drain::FinishPhase::Retarget);
             let mut req = if di == 0 {
